## Why this copy exists

LOGOS must ship a working KiCad MCP server. The upstream 0.1.0 release targets
KiCad 9 and, on KiCad 10, reports every ERC run as clean (violations moved into
`sheets[]`), refuses to export DRC reports for any board that has warnings, and
writes schematic files that KiCad cannot reopen in two cases. Patching the
host's editable install would disappear on reinstall and would not reach other
LOGOS deployments, so the patched tree is vendored here, under version control
and inside the release manifest.

## LOGOS patches on top of upstream 0.1.0

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/kicad_mcp_server/tools/validation.py` | `_collect_violations()` reads both ERC layouts (KiCad 9 top-level, KiCad 10 `sheets[]`) and drops excluded entries; `_generate_erc_report` / `_generate_drc_report` delete the stale report first and return `None` + message on failure; `get_*_violations` no longer infer success from `❌`/`⚠️` strings; `export_*_report` treat warnings as findings and create parent directories; a dangling label surfaces its name |
| `src/kicad_mcp_server/tools/schematic_editor.py` | `add_wire` splits multi-point input into two-point segments (a three-point `(wire (pts ...))` made the whole `.kicad_sch` unloadable); `_flatten_symbol_extends()` resolves library `extends` chains so derived symbols keep geometry and pins |
| `src/kicad_mcp_server/tools/netlist.py` | `trace_netlist_connection` formatter handles the per-net pin list returned for multi-pin components |
| `src/kicad_mcp_server/parsers/schematic_parser.py` | instance `(at ...)` parsed independently of file layout (positions were always `(0, 0)`) |
| `src/kicad_mcp_server/tools/project.py`, `src/kicad_mcp_server/utils/kicad_version.py` | `create_kicad_project` writes project-local `sym-lib-table` / `fp-lib-table` when the newest global KiCad table is empty; added `get_kicad_footprint_dir()` |

Nothing else was changed; `docs/` and `upstream-tests/` are upstream content.

